					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-146191#post-4397931</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-146191/scp-610#post-4397931</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sun, 13 Oct 2019 17:32:44 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Dr DeMarco</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2529617</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I'm in the camp of &quot;not aging very well&quot; about this SCP. The concept has a lot of potential, but also a distracting number of false leads: the map that doesn't show anything, the missing final log that was never intended to be a mystery (though it seems to have been retconned into one in the comments thread), and the vague/inappropriate status of the SCP. (That is, there doesn't seem to be any good reason to consider this Keter a &quot;neutralized threat&quot;.)</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Spoilers</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Spoilers</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p>Though the grammatical errors mentioned upthread seem to be mostly resolved, there's still a general haziness to the log writing: how many research teams are there? who escaped the church and how? why send a chunk of infectious material down an underground river to who knows where? why doesn't anyone have a name?</p> <p>I like the idea of the Lovecraftian underground civilization, but I think that sort of setting needs more description than it gets here.</p> </div> </div> </div> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
