					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-146191#post-3725348</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-146191/scp-610#post-3725348</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 01 Mar 2018 06:43:43 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>DrChandra</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1956625</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>610 is Yaldabaoth, the God<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-102389-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup> of the Sarkics, incarnated as pestilence.</p> <p>217 is Mehkane, the Broken God, incarnated as pestilence.</p> <p>The two gods hate each other and could never coexist, so a host could never sustain both for long. One would eventually route out the other. Which one? Yaldabaoth can grow like cancer, but it is driven only by animal instinct. Mekhane's mind is as cold and rational as the clockwork it's made from, plus it has a giant hammer.</p> <div class="footnotes-footer"> <div class="title">Footnotes</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-102389-1"><a href="javascript:;" >1</a>. Though Sarkics don't actively worship it, viewing themselves as parasites and Yaldabaoth as their host.</div> </div> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
